From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Berg <github@slipsprogrammor.no>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:49:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] 9849: MzLoader: start a segment block at its lowest far
 CALL/JMP target

MzLoader: add tests for segment block starts

adjustSegmentStarts() cuts a segment block after the last FAR RETURN
(CB) in its first paragraph. That misses a previous segment ending in
RETF n or a jump, and cuts into a far-called function that returns
within the paragraph. The tests for those cases fail until the next
commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

MzLoader: start a segment block at its lowest far CALL/JMP target

Code segments are often only word aligned, so a segment's code can
start a few bytes into its paragraph, and the bytes before it belong
to the previous segment. adjustSegmentStarts() moved them only after
a FAR RETURN (CB) in the block's first 16 bytes. It missed segments
whose predecessor ends in RETF n or a jump, and cut into far-called
functions that return within 16 bytes.

The target of a relocated CALLF/JMPF ptr16:16 (9A/EA) is code of its
segment. Take the lowest per segment, and cut after the last CB
before it in the first paragraph, or at it when it lies in that
paragraph and no CB precedes it. A target at offset 0 keeps the
block whole.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
